claims.claim:
Ley 1581 Art. 23 sanctions, imposed by the SIC:
- fines up to 2,000 SMMLV, which can repeat while the breach continues;
- suspension of data processing for up to 6 months;
- temporary closure if the ordered fixes are not made;
- immediate closure for sensitive data.

The 2026 SMMLV is COP 1,750,905 (Decrees 1469/1470 of 2025). The Consejo de Estado provisionally suspended the decree, and Decreto 0159 (Feb 2026) kept the value transitionally. That puts the nominal cap near COP 3.5 billion. Under Ley 1955/2019 Art. 49 such amounts are computed in UVT (COP 52,374 in 2026), so the actual peso cap may be lower.

design_implications:
CONSENT LEDGER (Prisma, append-only). One row per consent event:
- contact id and phone (E.164);
- purpose (e.g. PROMO_WHATSAPP, GROUP_MEMBERSHIP_NUMBER_VISIBLE, ORDER_PROCESSING);
- channel (whatsapp / web / checkout);
- source (Shopify checkbox, click-to-WhatsApp, QR on package, reply keyword);
- exact text version shown (store the full text or a hash plus a versioned template id);
- privacy-policy URL and version;
- the customer's reply content and WhatsApp message id (wamid);
- UTC timestamp, with America/Bogota for display.
Never update rows in place; revocations are new events. This is the proof the SIC can demand (Ley 1581 Arts. 9, 17(b); DUR 2.2.2.25.2.5).

SEND GATE (enforced in the queue worker, not only in the UI), applied to every promotional message including group or channel posts. Allow only if all of these hold:
- an active PROMO consent exists;
- no later revocation;
- the number is not in the RNE, checked recently, with the check timestamp stored;
- local time is Mon–Fri 07:00–19:00 or Sat 08:00–15:00 America/Bogota;
- it is not a Sunday or a Colombian public holiday (keep a holiday table, including holidays moved to Monday under the Ley Emiliani);
- a conservative frequency cap holds: no more than 1 promo per person per day and 1 channel per week.
Outside the window, messages are queued, never dropped. Customer-initiated 1:1 order conversations with the AI agent are arguably not 'advertising'. Still, have the agent avoid sending new promotional offers outside the hours.

